  "details": "When trying to play VRChat this morning (Europe time), the game constantly started crashing. Sometimes after about 30 seconds, sometimes after a few minutes.\n\nI have the following info on it:\n\n- Happened both in VR and Desktop mode\n\n- Happened both on Open beta and stable (VR only tested in stable)\n\n- Happened in home world and other world with people\n\n- Happened despite disabling essentially all avatars apart from voices using a custom safety setting.\n\n- Crash behavior was VRChat freezing.\n\n- Happened after a restart and restarting the router.\n\n- Happened with different avatars.\n\n- Happened after clearing the cache.\n\n- VRChat seems to have frozen for a split second every few minutes when an AmplitudeAPI error was written into the console.\n\n- Happened on my Windows 10 PC with an i9 9900k CPU and a 3070ti Gfx card\n\n- Did not happen on my Laptop with an AMD Ryzen 5 5600H CPU and a RTX 3050 Ti Gfx card.\n\n- Did not happen on my phone.\n\n- Did not happen before, when I tried rejoining a few hours later on Desktop.\n\nA few others seemed to have the same issue (From the VRChat Discord):\n\nhttps://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/189511567539306508/1292331360370819073\n\nhttps://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/1292374106125242410/1292374106125242410\n\nhttps://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/1292356645162319953/1292356645162319953\n\nhttps://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/189511567539306508/1292354914059550770",
